# ============================================================================
# SNIPER RUN SETTINGS (read by deploy/sniper-cron.sh on the server)
#
# Plain English:
#   This file decides what the sniper runs on the server. Change it here in
#   GitHub, the build publishes it, and within ~2 minutes the server restarts
#   the sniper with the new settings. Nobody needs to open a terminal.
#
#   SNIPER_ENABLED=0 stops everything (kill switch). 1 runs it.
#   SNIPER_MODE lists the programs to run (paper, feed-watch).
#   SNIPER_OUT_<MODE> sets that program's output folder (else SNIPER_OUT).
#   The sniper is PAPER ONLY: it holds no keys and cannot send transactions.
#   Only simple KEY=VALUE lines starting with SNIPER_ are used.
#
# PLANNED RUN 12 (NOT active: the values below this block are unchanged).
# MORNING SEQUENCE (each run.env change needs the owner's go-ahead):
#   1) Engine trial on the server, paper bot untouched (30 min):
#        cd ~/sniper-bin && bash deploy/sniper-engine.sh trial
#      It ends with "ENGINE TRIAL VERDICT: ..." (also in ~/sniper-engine/).
#      Why: the dex bot's identical engine mode needed ~2.1M node reads a
#      day live; ours has 3,000 paid a day and was only tested on a fake node.
#   2) Verdict WORKS: set the engine + feed wake-up lines below.
#   3) Any other verdict: do NOT set SNIPER_ENGINE. Run 12 is then:
#        SNIPER_OUT=paper-out/run12
#        SNIPER_YOUNG_TEST=1
#      plus the free WebSocket estimate, which is ON by default
#      (SNIPER_WS_HOT_ESTIMATE; status line "ws estimate", report section
#      "hot-pool WebSocket"). If it says FITS the spare node budget after a
#      few hours, also:
#        SNIPER_WS_HOT=1                pushed swaps for the ~400 hot pools
#   Live trading stays off either way.
# If the trial passes, set these lines:
#   SNIPER_OUT=paper-out/run12          new folder: clean numbers
#   SNIPER_ENGINE=1                     sniper's own engine; the cron starts
#                                       it (and restarts it if it dies or its
#                                       socket goes dead) before the paper bot
#   SNIPER_ENGINE_CHECK=1               side-by-side: trades use the node's quotes
#   SNIPER_FEED_WAKE=1                  rushes found from the sequencer feed
#   SNIPER_RHC_POLL_MS_WHEN_FEED=0      node still polled at today's pace
#   SNIPER_FEED_STALE_SECS=5            no feed frame for 5 s = back to polling
#   SNIPER_YOUNG_TEST=1                 pools under SNIPER_MIN_POOL_AGE_SECS get
#                                       a separate paper test group (2 slots of
#                                       $50, never live, own report section)
# ============================================================================
SNIPER_ENABLED=1
SNIPER_MODE=paper
# Run 13 (Nov 19 morning): fresh folder so $100 auto sizing, the WebSocket
# budget change and temporary young-pool blocks are measured cleanly (run 12
# ended +$50.72 / 109 trades main, 0 rugs; young group +$147 / 352, 11 rugs).
# Trap check still runs before every buy, so an empty blocklist is safe.
SNIPER_OUT=paper-out/run13
SNIPER_TP_PCT=5
SNIPER_SL_PCT=5
SNIPER_HOLD_SECS=60
# 1 = paper trader uses the paid Chainstack node (only while the arb bot is paused)
SNIPER_USE_CHAINSTACK=1
# Run 6: Uniswap V3 + V4 + V2, up to 3 positions (never 2 in one token,
# $150 open max). The node is asked once a second (~173k requests a day);
# push (every log billed by Chainstack) stays off unless SNIPER_PUSH=1.
SNIPER_VENUES=v3,v4,v2
SNIPER_MAX_POSITIONS=3
# Nov 19: auto size may go to $100 in deep pools (paper). Size study on the
# same trades: run 11 AUTO up to $100 +$281 vs $50 flat +$176; run 12 +$82 vs
# +$53. Auto still only picks a size whose instant round trip loses <= 1.5%.
SNIPER_MAX_USD=100
SNIPER_MAX_TOTAL_USD=300
SNIPER_RHC_POLL_MS=1000
# Speed step 1 (Nov 17): poll every 0.4 s from 8 PM to 8 AM Toronto, when
# the money is made. Delay test: a 2-block-slower buy kept 86% of profit,
# 10 blocks kept 52%. Adds ~130k node requests a day (~300k total, plan ~650k).
SNIPER_RHC_POLL_NIGHT_MS=400
SNIPER_NIGHT_HOURS=20-8
# Run 7: rug guard. Skip pools younger than 2 minutes (every run-5 rug was
# < 2 min; scored on run 5: +$307 net), block the creators of coins that
# rug or fail the trap check, and log creator/bundle shares to score later.
# Run 9: 10-minute age rule. Run 8's two rugs waited 3-4 min to dodge the
# 2-min rule; on runs 5-8 the 10-min rule + coin cutoff turn -$196 into
# about +$406 (scored on the same data, so an upper bound).
# Run 10: 2-HOUR age rule. Real pool ages for all 2,690 past trades: all
# 32 rugs were in pools under 1 hour old; pools 2 h+ had 0 rugs and
# +$800 (sim dollars). Pools the bot did not see being created now get
# their real birth looked up (paper-out/pool_births.json), not assumed old.
# Stop-loss 10% -> 5% (run 9 study, 294 trades: +$191 vs +$139).
# Run 11 (Nov 17): 1-HOUR age rule. The 2 h rule blocked every trade from
# 10 AM to 9 PM Nov 17 (426 of 429 V3 rushes were on pools < 2 h old).
# Pools 1-2 h old: 0 rugs in both studies (409 + 106 trades), +$73 and +$69.
# Speed step 1 also starts with run 11 (night polling, parallel quotes,
# delay logging).
SNIPER_MIN_POOL_AGE_SECS=3600
# Run 10b: before each start the cron catches up V4 pool keys created since
# the last history read (fixes most "unknown v4 pool" skips). Same run folder.
# V4 history read done (Nov 16): 746,757 tradeable V4 pools in
# paper-out/v4_pool_keys.json, loaded at start (restart to pick it up).
# Run 8: sell decisions on the REAL sale quote (not the chart), coin
# cutoff (skip a coin that lost over $15 in 6 h), and a measure-only study
# of tighter stops (-3/-5/-7%) recorded on every trade.
# Run 10: coin cutoff OFF (0). On 2 h+ pools it benched the hot coins
# that carry the profit: +$800 with no cutoff vs -$432 with the $15 one.
SNIPER_COIN_CUT_USD=0
# Run 10c: skip a coin's first rush in an hour (need 1 rush in the hour
# before). Past 2 h+ trades: first rushes 49 trades, 24% wins, -$54.
SNIPER_MIN_PRIOR_RUSHES=1
SNIPER_COIN_CUT_HOURS=6
# The separate feed server (sniper-feed, i-0c508651607bfb5cd) publishes its
# report on the private network; the main server adds it to the GitHub issue.
# Feed reader asks the free node for swaps once a second (not every 0.5 s):
# fewer 429 refusals, and the node still confirms every swap.
SNIPER_FW_POLL_MS=1000
# Main server's feed reader: feed from the feed server's relay (private
# network), swaps pushed by Chainstack (SNIPER_USE_CHAINSTACK).
SNIPER_RHC_FEED=ws://172.31.11.117:9642
SNIPER_OUT_FEED_WATCH=feed-out/main1
SNIPER_REMOTE_REPORT=http://172.31.11.117:8080/status.txt

# Run 12 (Nov 18, 11:30 AM): FAST PATH = hot-pool WebSocket (dex bot's proven
# approach). Engine trial failed the same way the dex bot's feed-mode copy did
# (0 of 10 hot-pool quotes answered, "dirty", in the first 5 minutes), so the
# engine and feed wake-up stay OFF. Free estimate before switching on: hot set
# ~23 pools + 31 V4 ids = ~112-141k pushed messages/day vs ~300k/day spare.
# Budget brake (wshot.rs) halves the hot list if the estimate goes over
# SNIPER_WS_HOT_BUDGET_DAY. Polling stays on as backup at its normal pace.
SNIPER_WS_HOT=1
# Nov 19: budget 250k -> 320k, paid for by slowing backup polling at night
# from 0.4 s to 0.6 s while the WebSocket is healthy (~-140k/day at the
# night rate). Polling still finds 2 of 3 rushes, so only a modest slow-down.
SNIPER_WS_HOT_BUDGET_DAY=320000
SNIPER_RHC_POLL_MS_WHEN_WS=600
# Cost fix (Nov 18, 5 PM): at noon the WebSocket ran ~373k/day (total node
# ~680k/day, over plan) because a few bot-churned pools push thousands of
# swaps an hour and are almost never traded. Pools busier than this many swaps
# a minute stay off the WebSocket (polling still watches them). If the brake
# hits its floor and the estimate is still over budget, the WebSocket pauses
# itself (polling does everything) until the estimate is under half budget.
# 9:30 PM Nov 18: raised 20 -> 60. At 20, 2 of 3 rushes were found by polling
# (1,034 vs 565): rushing pools crossed 20 swaps/min and dropped off the
# WebSocket right when it mattered. Cost was ~161k/day vs 250k budget; the
# brake and off switch still guard the bill.
SNIPER_WS_HOT_MAX_SWAPS_PER_MIN=60
# Young-pool test group: pools under 1 h traded on paper in their own 2 slots,
# reported separately, never live. Main results exclude them.
SNIPER_YOUNG_TEST=1
